      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a draft for your memo. It's professional, friendly, and gets straight to the point about ergonomic setup. Remember, even small adjustments can make a big difference in preventing aches and pains, which is a lot easier than trying to fix a long-term issue later on.\n\n***\n\n**Subject: Quick Tip: Keeping Your Remote Workstation Ergonomic!**\n\nHi Team,\n\nAs we continue working remotely, I wanted to send a friendly reminder about setting up your home workstations for maximum comfort and health. A quick check on your ergonomic setup can prevent those nagging wrist or neck pains that can creep up on you during a long day. Please take a few minutes this week to ensure your chair height and monitor positioning are optimized for you.\n\n**Key Checks:**\n\n*   **Chair Height:** Adjust your chair so your feet are flat on the floor and your knees are at roughly a 90-degree angle.\n*   **Monitor Level:** Your monitor screen should be positioned so the top third of the screen is at or slightly below eye level.\n\nTaking these small steps is a huge investment in your long-term well-being. If you need resources or have questions about adjusting your setup, please don",
